    "['no shutdown', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false\\nset interfaces ge-2/0/0 disable false\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, `no shutdown` (Cisco) is equivalent to enabling an interface by setting `disable false`.\\n- The command structure follows Juniper's hierarchical format using the `set` command.\\n- I've included both interface translations since both interfaces had the same `no shutdown` command in the original config.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-2/0/0 disable false', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false\\nset interfaces ge-2/0/0 disable false\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, `no shutdown` (Cisco) is equivalent to enabling an interface by setting `disable false`.\\n- The command structure follows Juniper's hierarchical format using the `set` command.\\n- I've included both interface translations since both interfaces had the same `no shutdown` command in the original config.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-2/0/0 disable false'}]]": 1,
